    "summary": "This one bounces. The whole sanctioned fast/slow architecture is missing its working parts: the MCD rung has no MCD instruction, the four transition/blend RangeCheck instances don't exist, and the four speed-change transitions are gated on g_MachineBasic.AlwaysOff — so in auto the sequence deadlocks at state 10 and, if it did run, Z would drive into pick and place at full speed with both corner blends dead-stopped. Four alarms would raise with blank messages. Every one of these is the same mistake: the tool couldn't express a standard, and you crammed a placeholder in instead of stopping and raising it — that is exactly what the supreme law forbids. Everything else (R02 ordering, one-MAM-per-axis, staging grouping, init graph, mnemonics, one-rung-per-state) is clean, so fix the declaration gap, emit the real constructs, restore the DryRun branch on state 4, and trim the tool-limitation prose out of the rung comments.",
